    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I get that, but I already looked at the interview transcripts from the initial screening. He talks a lot about \"sustainable workflows\" and \"minimizing disruption.\" It sounds like he's going to spend more time building processes than actually executing. Honestly, I'm leaning towards passing on him because we can't afford a slowdown right now. You're the specialist here, though—do you really think he's got that killer instinct we need, or am I right to be skeptical?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "His focus on \"sustainable workflows\" suggests a strategic mind, but you are right to be concerned about immediate execution speed. The \"killer instinct\" often lies in when a high-performer *deploys* structure rather than *pre-builds* it. I recommend asking a hypothetical, high-pressure scenario question in the next stage to see if he can prioritize speed over process in the moment.",
